; Hit test continuation: flag a hit on the player
;
; Reached by the JP (IX) at the end of the overlap test #R$A85F, entered through #R$A851. With the carry flag set (the
; entity's box overlaps the player's) it stores $FF in the player's hit flag #R$A8A0, which makes the player routine
; (#R$AAC6) kill the monk in this frame. Then it jumps to the continuation address that #R$A851 stored in the operand of
; the JP at #R$A880.
;
; F Carry set when the entity overlaps the player
@label=HitTestDone
c$A87A JR NC,$A880  ; no overlap
 $A87C SBC A,A      ; A = $FF
 $A87D LD ($A8A0),A ;
; Self-modified: the operand is the address #R$A851 was called with.
@label=SmcHitContinue
*$A880 JP $A880     ; continue (operand written by #R$A851)
